<title>UK: UK clears HBG, Gulf Canada bids.</title>
<headline>UK clears HBG, Gulf Canada bids.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Trade and Industry ministry said on Wednesday that after studies by the Office of Fair Trading it had decided to approve two proposed acquisitions by larger foreign firms of smaller British targets.</p>
<p>In a statement the ministry said it had decided not to refer for monopolies' investigation the proposed purchase by Dutch construction company Hollandsche Beton Groep NV of British building company Higgs and Hill Plc, and Gulf Canada Resources Ltd's bid to buy oil exploration group Clyde Petroleum Plc.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
